Description: Enumerates the distinct partitions produced as the resolution
    varies on a fixed graph. The Simple engine uses a deterministic visit
    order and can prune the resolution range using a cluster count bound.
    The Seurat engine tracks exact-arithmetic versions of the two Louvain
    algorithms in 'Seurat' 5.5, including comparisons between random starts
    at a fixed seed. Both engines can search disjoint intervals in parallel
    and store the retained partitions, resolution intervals and classical
    Newman-Girvan modularity scores in a Seurat object's tools slot.
